===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|la|blennius}}, {{m|la|blendius}}, from {{der|en|grc|βλεννός||mucus, slime}} (whence Modern Greek {{m|el|βλέννα}}), because of its slimy coating. From {{der|en|ine-pro|*mel-|t=soft}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈblɛni/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛni|s=2}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-blenny.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A {{vern|true blenny}}, any of various marine fishes from the suborder [[Blennioidei]] or order {{taxfmt|Blenniiformes|order}} that are generally small and elongated which dwell on the sea floor, including scaled and scaleless forms and dramatically divergent appearance, in several families.
## [[Blenniidae]] ([[combtooth blenny|combtooth blennies]])
## [[Chaenopsidae]] ({{vern|pikeblenny|pikeblennies}}, {{vern|tubeblenny|tubeblennies}}, and {{vern|flagblenny|flagblennies}})
## {{taxlink|Clinidae|family}} ([[weedfish]]es)
## {{taxlink|Dactyloscopidae|family}} ({{vern|sand stargazer|pl=s}})
## {{taxlink|Labrisomidae|family}} ([[labrisomid]]s)
## [[Tripterygiidae]] ({{vern|triple-fin blenny|triple-fin blennies}})
# A number of fish of similar appearance not closely related.
## {{vern|bartail blenny}} ({{taxlink|Platycephalus indicus|species}}, in family {{taxlink|Pseudochromidae|family}})
## {{l|en|viviparous blenny}} ({{taxfmt|Zoarces viviparus|species}}, in family [[Zoarcidae]])
## {{vern|convict blenny}}/{{vern|engineer blenny}} ({{taxlink|Pholidichthys leucotaenia|species}}, in family {{taxlink|Pholidichthyidae|family}})
## {{vern|scooter blenny}} ({{taxlink|Neosynchiropus ocellatus|species}}, in family [[Callionymidae]])

